course: dictionary
lesson: 6788
title: Orbit: a path around something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An orbit is the curved path that something follows as it goes around a bigger object, like a moon going around a planet. Orbit can also be a verb: to orbit is to move around something in a path like this. Context helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: «Most known asteroids orbit in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter.» Here orbit is a verb, because the asteroids are doing the action of moving around. Ask: what word would fit? Move around, or circle? Your clues show that orbit means moving around in a path.
explain: «A satellite in orbit is falling around the Earth while it moves sideways very fast.» Here orbit is a noun, the path the satellite follows. The words falling around and moves sideways are the clues. If you read the word as a place or a path, the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An orbit is the curved path a planet, moon or satellite follows around a star or planet.
fact: To orbit means to move around something in a path like this.
fact: The Earth orbits the Sun once a year, which is about 365 days.
fact: The Moon orbits the Earth about once a month.
fact: Satellites orbit the Earth to send TV signals and help with weather forecasts.
exercise: «A satnav or phone finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites in orbit.» What does in orbit mean here? | *Moving around the Earth in a curved path | Lost under the ground | Glowing in the dark | Stuck in a traffic jam
exercise: «The Earth orbits the Sun once a year.» About how long is one orbit of the Earth around the Sun? | About a week | About a day | *About 365 days | About an hour
exercise: Ravi says orbit means to sit still in one place. What does orbit mean? | *To move around something in a path | To sit still in one place | To sleep under a blanket | To shout loudly
test: «The Great Wall is very long but only a few metres wide, and astronauts said they could not see it with the naked eye from orbit.» What does orbit mean in this sentence? | *The path a spacecraft follows around the Earth | A kind of bird that flies south | A deep hole in the ground | A loud noise
test: «The Moon orbits the Earth about once a month.» What does orbits mean here? | Falls straight down to the ground | Stops at the edge of the Earth | *Goes round the Earth in a curved path | Shines brightly in the sky
exam: What does «falling around the Earth while it moves sideways very fast» tell us about a satellite in orbit? | It stops moving after one day | It is always perfectly still | *It keeps falling around the Earth while moving sideways fast | It is stuck to the ground
